{"1218230": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Rhythmic Retro Racer", "steam_appid": 1218230, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h1>Update Notes</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/extras/e01e0e0a14f2fcce7247a4279ae68d2c.avif?t=1784220761\" width=1560 height=878 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >v 2 </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Patch Notes – Major Update</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>New Scenario</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game now includes a <strong>new narrative layer</strong>, expanding the original story.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Environmental storytelling has been reworked to support the updated scenario.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Subtle narrative clues and unsettling moments have been added across the experience.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rhythm System Upgrade</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rhythm sequences have been <strong>re-authored using professional beatmapping tools (Arrow Vortex)</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Timing, note density, and structure are now more precise and consistent with the soundtrack.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Improved synchronization between audio, visuals, and player input.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Atmosphere &amp; Flow</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Improved pacing in key sequences.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Minor visual and audio adjustments to strengthen immersion.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fixes &amp; Improvements</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Various stability and performance improvements.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Minor bug fixes and polish.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >if you experiencing any problem please contact us</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><a href=\"mailto:berzahgames@gmail.com\">berzahgames@gmail.com</a></p></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/extras/9f4a12c01666e4d81543cd641909a483.avif?t=1784220761\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/extras_big/9f4a12c01666e4d81543cd641909a483.avif?t=1784220761 width=1560 height=802 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>Note:</strong> Developed by a solo developer. Thank you for your patience, support, and constructive feedback—it truly helps make the game better.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rhythmic Retro Racer</strong> is a music-focused rhythm game built around carefully authored timing and atmosphere. The game takes place in a mysterious room inspired by 90s retro aesthetics, where you select VHS tapes and enter structured rhythm sequences. The room is not a menu — it is part of the narrative.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At its core, the gameplay focuses on <strong>precisely authored rhythm patterns</strong>, created using professional rhythm composition tools. Notes are not randomly generated or loosely synced. Each sequence is intentionally designed to match the structure, intensity, and flow of the soundtrack.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The soundtrack is a central pillar of the experience. Powerful synthwave tracks drive both gameplay and mood, while visuals, pacing, and tension are shaped around the music rather than reacting to it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game also features a dedicated <strong>Race Mode</strong>, expanding the experience beyond traditional rhythm gameplay. Players can choose between 8 different cars, compete across multiple race maps, earn money through races, and unlock new vehicles through an in-game purchase system. While still connected to the game’s retro atmosphere and soundtrack-driven identity, Race Mode offers a more arcade-focused experience built around speed, progression, and replayability.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you progress, subtle narrative elements and unsettling moments begin to surface. Without explicit exposition, the game slowly reveals that what you are doing is not entertainment, but part of a larger, uneasy experiment. The sense of control fades, replaced by curiosity, tension, and discomfort.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rhythmic Retro Racer</strong> blends rhythm gameplay with psychological tension, retro-futuristic atmosphere, and a mysterious narrative that unfolds through play — not dialogue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a game about music, precision, and the feeling that something is not quite right.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/extras/9f4a12c01666e4d81543cd641909a483.avif?t=1784220761\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/extras_big/9f4a12c01666e4d81543cd641909a483.avif?t=1784220761 width=1560 height=802 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>Note:</strong> Developed by a solo developer. Thank you for your patience, support, and constructive feedback—it truly helps make the game better.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rhythmic Retro Racer</strong> is a music-focused rhythm game built around carefully authored timing and atmosphere. The game takes place in a mysterious room inspired by 90s retro aesthetics, where you select VHS tapes and enter structured rhythm sequences. The room is not a menu — it is part of the narrative.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At its core, the gameplay focuses on <strong>precisely authored rhythm patterns</strong>, created using professional rhythm composition tools. Notes are not randomly generated or loosely synced. Each sequence is intentionally designed to match the structure, intensity, and flow of the soundtrack.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The soundtrack is a central pillar of the experience. Powerful synthwave tracks drive both gameplay and mood, while visuals, pacing, and tension are shaped around the music rather than reacting to it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game also features a dedicated <strong>Race Mode</strong>, expanding the experience beyond traditional rhythm gameplay. Players can choose between 8 different cars, compete across multiple race maps, earn money through races, and unlock new vehicles through an in-game purchase system. While still connected to the game’s retro atmosphere and soundtrack-driven identity, Race Mode offers a more arcade-focused experience built around speed, progression, and replayability.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you progress, subtle narrative elements and unsettling moments begin to surface. Without explicit exposition, the game slowly reveals that what you are doing is not entertainment, but part of a larger, uneasy experiment. The sense of control fades, replaced by curiosity, tension, and discomfort.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rhythmic Retro Racer</strong> blends rhythm gameplay with psychological tension, retro-futuristic atmosphere, and a mysterious narrative that unfolds through play — not dialogue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a game about music, precision, and the feeling that something is not quite right.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "Rhythmic Retro Racer is a music-first rhythm game set in a mysterious 90s retro room. Hit precisely crafted rhythms built with professional tools and lose yourself in a powerful synthwave soundtrack. As the tension grows, you realize you are not playing a game, you are part of an experiment.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/aab4f5b74ee479e8cdba4633ae7b91677fd19320/header.jpg?t=1784220761", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/1ab92fc2f20b154a2eae8f5fa6ce4dfbfb3ee611/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1784220761", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1218230/1ab92fc2f20b154a2eae8f5fa6ce4dfbfb3ee611/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1784220761", "website": "https://berzahgames.com/", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> windows 7<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i5<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> gtx 970 will work, works 60fps @RTX 3050</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> windows 7,8,10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i7<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Better visual performance on rtx 2080 and more</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\">